  "text": "ParLiament House\nCANBERRA•\nJune 9th. 1955.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nI would like to extend my heartiest\ncongratulations on the honour\nconferred upon jou to-day•\nIt must be very gratifying to feel\nthat\nafter\nall these years, your\nservices have been recognised by\nHer Majesty the Queen.\nYours sincerely,\n(GEORGE McLEAY)\nSensitter.\nMr. C. H. McFadyen, C.B.E•,\nsecretary,\nDepartment of Shipping & Transport,\nMELBOURNE •\nC.1.",
